  {
    "key": "mock.zimsec.paper-2",
    "kind": "MOCK_EXAM",
    "title": "Mock exam in the style of ZIMSEC O-Level Mathematics Paper 2",
    "description": "A full-length practice paper modelled on ZIMSEC O-Level Mathematics Paper 2: compulsory structured questions in Section A and a choice of longer questions in Section B, 2 hours 30 minutes, 100 marks. Questions are drawn from the question bank, so every attempt is a new paper. This is an original practice paper written for this platform in the style of the real examination. It is not an official ZIMSEC paper, and its questions are not past-paper questions.",
    "instructions": "Answer **all** the questions in Section A and **any eight** questions in Section B. You have 2 hours 30 minutes.\n\n- Section A is worth 52 marks and Section B 48 marks (eight questions of 6 marks). If you answer more than eight questions in Section B, your best eight count.\n- You may use a calculator in this paper. Give answers that are not exact to three significant figures, and angles in degrees to one decimal place, unless the question says otherwise.\n- Show your working: method marks are given for correct working even when the final answer is wrong.\n- The paper is marked when you submit or when the time runs out. You then see your score, a grade estimate and worked solutions.\n\nIn the real Paper 2, Section B has fewer and longer questions, and you choose three of them. This practice paper uses shorter questions from the bank with the same total marks and time, and still lets you choose, so it practises the same skills and pacing. Check the instructions on your own examination papers for the current 4004 syllabus.",
